model Qwen3.5-0.8B; operands fp16 in / f32 accumulate / 16-bit C (see the
constraint at the bottom). rate = 6.885 TFLOP/s and bandwidth =
240.0 GB/s, BOTH QUOTED from devices/ — neither is measured by this script.
ridge = rate / bandwidth = 28.69 flops per byte = 0.03486 bytes per flop.
A shape below the ridge is bandwidth-bound however good the kernel is; that is a statement
about the shape, not about the route. Byte columns are the MINIMUM traffic (each operand
touched once); a badly blocked kernel re-reads A per N-tile and W per M-tile, so real
numbers can only be worse than what is printed.

flop accounting: 0.9952 GFLOP per token in block matmuls (186 matmuls), + 0.5086 GFLOP per priced logits row.
The plan divides its ceilings by ~1.6 GFLOP/token; the matmul part alone is 1.5038 GFLOP/token when every token's logits are priced,
and prefill prices ONE row per request (§06.5), so the prefill figure is the block part.

