=== epilogue bill: what a library matmul unfuses, in extra bytes per wave
  'fused today' is what the engine already does inside the matmul kernel.
  site                              fused today?                    M=64       M=512      M=1024      M=3072
  silu(gate)*up (mlp_gateup)        yes — inside the GEMM         42 MiB     336 MiB     672 MiB   1.969 GiB
  attn gate de-interleave           no — attn_prep is its own         0 B         0 B         0 B         0 B
  q/k head-norm + rope              no — attn_prep is its own         0 B         0 B         0 B         0 B
  gdn gated RMSNorm (§04.5)         no — own kernel already          0 B         0 B         0 B         0 B
  residual add + next RMSNorm       no — glue is its own pass         0 B         0 B         0 B         0 B
  Only the MLP costs anything. `mlp_gateup` writes `act` once; a library gate+up writes both
  halves (2 tiles), a silu-mul kernel reads both (2 tiles) and writes act (1 tile) = 5 tiles
  of M x 3584 x 2 B per layer instead of 1. Concatenating gate|up into one [7168,1024] weight
  merges the two calls but does NOT change that count — it buys launches, not traffic.
  The three attention/GDN epilogues are already separate passes reading a matmul output that
  is already written to memory, so a library matmul changes nothing there.

  What the library route gives BACK: `proj_gemv` runs PACK_X=false and so needs F32
  activations, which is most of why 115 cast launches per token exist (engine/kernels_proj.cpp,
  `engine/results.md` E2). A library GEMM taking a 16-bit A operand reads what glue wrote, so
  those casts disappear for the projections — a launch-and-dispatch saving at the measured
  dispatch floor, not a traffic one.

  CONSTRAINT no shape table can express — the rounding point. Every shipped pin rounds a
  projection's product to BF16 where the reference does, so a library call must be given a
  16-bit C dtype (HIPBLAS_COMPUTE_32F with C bf16/fp16). Asking for F32 C would both double
  the activation traffic above and move a rounding, and a moved rounding is a route change
  (D-3/D-5), not a tuning knob.
